bugs in CASEx, SKPC, and RET instructions that HCORE test missed.   HCORE 
tests showed that all instructions passed instead.  Indeed, AXE test suite
is much-needed.  I am looking for that.

About OpenVMS 7.2, I tried to boot it but it always stalls after RQDX3
initialization and units scanned (during estimated step 40 according to 
VAX internal and data structure handbook).  I took a copy of
system disk image from my PicoVAX emulator to try my VAX emulator.  It
resulted the different.  After RQDX3 initialization and unit scanned
with interrupt enabled, it randomly read blocks from system disk as 
processes were spawned or forked to read blocks in parallel ways.
Then it stalled somewhere.  I am trying to explain you about steps
that my debug.log showed.

My debug log showed to boot installation OpenVMS CD:

>>> b dua1

* Loaded and run VMB
* VMB loaded and run SYSBOOT]
* SYSBOOT loaded several images into memory then transferred its control
  to OpenVMS to continue boot.
* OpenVMS tested some instructions for emulation.
* OpenVMS announced banner information (OpenVMS version X72T...)
* OpenVMS initialized RQDX3 controller as primitive routines
* OpenVMS loaded several more images
* OpenVMS created null job process and start its execution.
* OpenVMS re-initialized RQDX3 controller and scanned units for existing
  medium, etc.  Also enabled interrupts during RQDX3 initialization.
* Stalled here (every few seconds, checked RQDX3 to make sure everything 
  ok) forever....

I have a copy of disk system from my PicoVAX emulator and tried that.

[Same results until 2nd RQDX3 initialization]
* After 2nd RQDX3 initialization and scanned units for existing medium
  storage, then randomly read several blocks as loading images in 
  parallel.
* Stalled here (every few seconds, checked RQDX3 to make sure everything
  ok) forever....

However, NetBSD/vax booted fine and I was able logged into system.

Thank you!

