It sounds like the VAXStation TCP/IP database has never been configured.
If it had, you'd be able to see the version and the IP address:

  $ ucx
  UCX> show version

  Digital TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS VAX Version V4.2 - ECO 3
  on a VAXstation 4000-96 running OpenVMS V7.1

  UCX> show interface
                                                       Packets
  Interface   IP_Addr         Network mask      Receive          Send     MTU

   ZE0        209.16.45.102   255.255.255.248    794934        825357    1500
   LO0        127.0.0.1       255.0.0.0               0             0   65535
  UCX>

The documentation for Digital TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS is available at:

    http://www.openvms.compaq.com:8000/#tcpip   

You'll need the "Compaq TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS Installation and 
Configuration" manual.

This command starts the configuration:

   $@SYS$MANAGER:UCX$CONFIG

--Jerry Leslie     (my opinions are strictly my own)


