Might want to take a look at the Installation Guide on the documentation
CD. Assuming you are installing from the Tru64 CD kit. All you need is a
PC and a webbrowser to read them.

Back when I was working with DUNIX 4.0d, Advanced Filesystem (AdvFS)
used to be a seprately installed and licensed package. Typically, AdvFS
was on one of the 'Associated Products' CD's. The license was included
on the old educational license contracts. Not sure if it's in the
non-commercial version. Otherwise you'll need to spend some money.

The Installation Guide on the documentation CD had instructions on how
to install AdvFS. Basically, it said little more than 'find the AFA
directory and install with setld'. Find the AFA directory on the
associated products CD and read the README file.

So, for fun I headed over to Compaq's Tru64 site to see if they still
kept the docs online. Looks like they do:
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/pub_page/doc_list.html
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/pub_page/V40F_DOCS.HTM

And here's the section in 4.0f that mentions AdvFS (all one line):
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40F_HTML/AQTLGCTE/LYRDPRDX.HTM#polycenter-advfs-utils-sect

And here's the 4.0f CD-ROM contents which tells you which disk it's on:
http://www.tru64unix.compaq.com/docs/base_doc/DOCUMENTATION/V40F_HTML/SUPPDOCS/CDLIST.HTM

Quickly scanning the docs, it looks like things did not change much
between 4.0d and 4.0f.

Have fun!

