Perfectly acceptable... AFAIK, this group is for all things DEC
(hardware, OSes, marketing fallacies)...
 
> I recently acquired a Digital alphastation 255 and I am wondering if
> someone knows how to remove it's (complete) front panel.
> 
> Thank you.
> 
> //Regards, Johan.

1. Remove the system's lid (loosen screw on back, pull straight back on
lid and up).

2. Remove the sides exposing the front panel's side clips:

	a. The side closest to the CPU is removed by pushing in
	behind the tab next to the CPU fan cage and pulling back
	on the side (note the diagram...Push there).

	b. The side closes to the CDROM is removed easily by simply
	pulling back and out.

3. Remove the floppy/hdrive mount to expose the front panel's center
clips:

	a. Disconnect all cables from the floppy and hard drive. 
	The floppy/hdrive mount is held in place with two tabs. Push 
	in on the tabs while pulling the mount back and up. It should 
	all come out in one piece.

4. Carefully pry up one set of the front panel's side tabs, then release
the center tabs. The other set should release easily at that point.

Installation is reversed.

Becareful. All the panels have various little plastic tabs which are
easily sheared off. 

