  Um, do you really want something that old, that big, that heavy, that 
  amp-hungry, and that glacially slow?  The VAX-11/725, VAX-11/730, 
  VAX-11/750 and (the rarely seen) VAX-11/751 are all exceedingly 
  ancient VAX boxes.

  Is there any particular feature you are looking for?  (The only common
  thread I see connecting these four VAX systems is the availability of 
  Unibus I/O and the use of MS750 memory.  There are other and far more 
  recent VAX systems -- well, relatively speaking :-) -- that also offer 
  Unibus connectivity, and any local availability of MS650 boards probably 
  isn't the best reason to seek such ancient VAX systems.

  OpenVMS VAX no longer supports any of the VAX-11/7xx series systems.

  I would strongly encourage you to look for a VAXstation 4000, or any
  of the other (far) more recent VAX systems.  These are far faster, far 
  more flexible, far smaller, far easier to connect to SCSI storage and
  to far more than a pittance of physical memory, and are also far less 
  amp-starved.  Oh, and parts are easier to find...


