insects it could print wonders in both cases too.

Time passed and the KDF9 became extinct and was replaced by a greater
beast called 1906A. This evolutionary backstep used punched cards
which had upper case only and no tabs and printed its output thus
also. The high priests were permitted to speak to the great beast via
Tele Types, and the Great High Priest had a VDU, but these too spoke
only upper case. So many a PhD thesis had to be produced in other
ways. Moreover, the great beast-tamer spoke thus: "Al Gol doth cause
the mighty 1906A much travail in translation. Therefore we will teach
the twin tribes of Scien Tists and Engi Neers to speak For Tran which
is a greatly better language spoken the world over, and everyone else
shall speak Co Bol which is better still. But you will still only have
upper case".

More time passed, and behold there appeared little beasts conceived by
great gods with names to inspire awe such as DEC (which in latter days
did adopt the bar-full name of d|i|g|i|t|a|l and was consumed by
Compaq causing much sorrow and an upturn in the sackcloth and ashes
industry), Data General (son of DEC), Hewlett-Packard, and Prime. They
too used Tele Types and spoke only upper case, but did have tabs. But
then rumours spread abroad of wonderful machines called DEC Writers
which had lower case letters (albeit without descenders). And yea
there was much delight in the eyes of graduate students who could use
computers to produce their theses once again, and much eyestrain
amongst external examiners who really would have liked descenders,
until the great Son of Ep gave us these too, and even colour graphics,
albeit spottily.

And the Tower of Babel was rebuilt and there came forth many different
operating systems and languages with great prophets who said:
"Herewith art a new way of life. All thou hast used before is rubbish
and thou must change thy ways. Repent and spend years redoing thy
life's work according unto my ways and thou shalt forever be able to
produce more efficiently." Which the gullible fell for every time and
spent so much effort changing that they never did anything original
ever again.

Yet more time passed, and behold there came VDUs and laser printers
which not only had descenders but even more letters with strange hats
and beslashed. And external examiners suffered less eyestrain, except
when graduate students used too many fonts on one page.

In the end times, there came Bill Gates who declared himself the Only
True Prophet, added even more strange squiggles, and decreed: "Thou
shalt use graphical user interfaces and mayst have colour" (though
being from lands afar he bespake it "color"). "And thou canst have
