NTFS is not case insensitive -it's case sensitive.
It's case insensiitvity is a (typical MS) kludge opon NTFS by the WIN32
subsystem of the NT kernel (legacy reasons). Case insensitivity has
nothing, absolutely nothing to do with the NTFS filesystem.
Unix OSes witch implement case-insensitivity for NTFS are violating the
NTFS spec. per se ...  but they are supporting the expected filesystem
behaviour of nearly all applications.


> Case folding during comparisons just isn't desirable to do, except for legacy
