MatrixGear wrote:
> 
> Hi,
> 
> How do I get a DECStation to boot from CD-ROM drive?
> 
> I want to re-install ULTRIX.
> 
> Michael

boot (device name)

If the drive has SCSI ID 4 and it's on the first SCSI
controller then "boot dka400".  SCSI ID 0 is different,
it would be "boot dka0", not "boot dka000".

To see the devices do "show dev" at the console prompt.

The CD-ROM drive will need to be set for 512 byte blocks.
If you have a DEC RRD drive your OK.  If it came from a
PC it needs to be set for 512 byte blocks, not 2048, 
which is what most PC CD-ROM drives are set to.  If you 
can't set it to 512 byte blocks you can't boot from it.
Most CD-ROMs from early Unix workstations should work OK.

Robert


