In comp.sys.dec sword7@speakeasy.org wrote:
> However a few problems still need fixed.  During startup scripts, I got
> several segmentation fault errors but boot went so well.

Well, I looked into the root directory (/) in NetBSD/vax vdisk image and
found two core dumps - route.core and sleep.core.  I tried to execute
'sleep 10' and saw what happens...  I was able reproduce that error.

# sleep 10
Segmentation Fault

I entered GDB debugger and run it.  It crashed at loc 4CE9.

   4CE9 MOVL R0,B^08(AP)

It attempted to return results back to caller but ended up page fault
trap.  It attempted to put results into loc 0000000A.  That function
converted from ASCII numbers to integer.  I looked up at caller and found 
out that PUSHL S^#0A into SP -> 08(AP) before page fault trap at loc 2000
for page-in.  During page fault trap, it just enable pages into valid
and returned back to that 'sleep' program.

Kevin Hardy, do you know about that?

Thank you!

-- Tim Stark

