In article <fJG08.586$Na5.428419@paloalto-snr2.gtei.net>, dittman@dittman.net writes:

> I have a RaidArray 310 and just got a second HSZ20 controller.
> How do I connect it to the HSZ20 already in the RA310 for dual-
> redundant mode?
> 

   Good question.

   The RA310 was never supported in a dual-redundant configuration.

   It would be interesting to see if it's possible to convert it to
dual, but it seems like an onerous task. You'd need special SCSI
cables for starters ( with the extra headers for a second controller ).
It's been a while since I had one opened, up - I'm not sure there is
physical space in the box for the second controller or available
power connections.

  It seems you'd also need a way to change the SCSI id of the second
controller ( to a unit number other than 7 ). If you get these hardware
issues resolved the question would be if the software is clever enough
to deal with two controllers ( there seems to be latent support for
this in the firmware based on the command line help, but it may not
be usable ).

   I'd be interested in hearing your results on this, if you get
anywhere please report back here.



