There was a MAIL system in common use on TOPS-10 systems on the UK
academic JANET X25 network. User interface was a subset of TOPS-20 MM
but files were stored in a master spool directory with one file for
each PPN. The PPN was actually stored as the file name. Some students
figured out that these mail files were not protected by default and
used the PIP octal syntax for file names to just list them directly.
TYPE wouldn't work. .

