I disagree.  There should be no way to create a file that cannot be
referenced (displayed or specified) from the user interface.  If you provide
no limits on what a filename can be in the filesystem, then you must either
craft a very good and consistant way of specifying files, or you may need to
be able to allow a representation of characters that would cause ambiguity.

