provide a way to distinguish these two files.

However, many people feel that from a useabilty point of view, Foo.Bar and
foo.bar and FOO.BAR should all reference the same file.  But you can't do
this unambiguously if the filesystem permits case to be a distinction
between files of the same names, but with differing case.








