In point of fact, to use the VMS command line parsing requires the
application to make calls to parse the command line.  It isn't some
automatic magic.  From any language you can always make the call to simply
get the command line, and parse it yourself.

The C language handles the command line in the standard way, giving you argv
and argc... of course, it does do some silly but understandable things -
like lowercasing the entire line (except for quoted portions).  And even
that can be gotten around in recent VMS versions.






