Under TOPS-20 you could logout without performing an implicit expunge.
The expunge was just the default action. Can't remember offhand if the
expunge (deldf% I think) was performed by the EXEC command processor
or the lgout% jsys itself but it was possible to override.TOPS-20
would only remove deleted but not yet expunged files itself if the
space on the disk dropped below a critical threshold. In this case a
system message was broadcast to all logged in users worded something
like
[Diskspace low on structure PS: Starting Expunge of deleted files in
30 seconds]. Can't recall offhand if a program could enable a software
interrupt on this condition. 

