   By using a proper list syntax:

   delete something.x;*,something.c;*

   You gotta remember, DCL is NOT expanding wildcards here like a shell.
   The program is using standard library calls to loop over the wild
   card, and in the case of output file name wildcarding, it's using the
   related name concept.



