>> The second filespec doesn't specify a file, like the first filespec does.  The
>> second one represents a group of proposed filenames that are VERY DEPENDENT
>> upon the value of the first group.
>> 
>
>   The first file name specifies a collection of names, and so does the
>   second.  Just because someone taught you a different view point
>   doesn't make it so.
