Bob Koehler <koehler@encompasserve.org> wrote:
>   Same here, I've got several ksh scripts that take file name
>   parameters, but no matter how much I quote the original I can't
>   get past the spaces in all my Mac folder names.

Either take your arguments one by one like this:

while [ ".$1" != "."]
do
  frob "$1"
  shift
done

Or use this trick:

for i in ${1+"$@"}
do
  frob "$i"
done

I tend to use the first if I'm going to be parsing multi-word options, and
the latter otherwise.

