Simple...

RENAME *.c *.x

When renaming '*.c' to '*.x', the first '*.c' means something
very different from '*.x' (not just in the sense of the name
of the 'extension' (geesh, I hate that notion also.))

I used to like the 'DEC' CLI approach, writing my own DCL
on RSX11M before it was commonly available.   After seeing
the 'modal' inconsistancy, it became obviously clunky.

Luckily, massive renames aren't that common, and
very convienient availability of subdirectories can sometimes
be an equivalent tool (along with RCS) for version control
or file segregation.

When massive renames are needed, then the scripting schemes
can be used convieniently as subroutines.

John



