Generally, this means arcinst doesn't see the drive - or can't see it
clearly - which, I guess in this case would be the array you created. 
This can be caused by any standard disk/cable/controller problem.  

Can you see the array from the arc console?  What kind of array is it?
How did you change the channels connected to the internal storageworks
shelf?

Are there other drives connected to the other controllers?  Is the
target array still the first drive on the first scsi bus?

If this is all too confusing, I would take the system down to a single
disk in the top slot and a single controller, then configure the drive
as a JBOD with the SWXCRMGR or RA200RCU, check to make sure the drive
was in the system configuration, and try arcinst again.




  

