don't have a recent CD you can also find it at ftp.digital.com in
the /pub/DEC/Alpha/firmware/v6.1/utility/swxcrmgr directory.

   There's also a program in that directory (RA200FL) which will
do the updating. If you need a copy of the configuration program
it's in there also (RA200RCU.EXE)

   (You may already know the following, but in case you don't here
are the instructions for performing the update on an Alpha ).

   There should be several versions of the image in that directory, 
called swxcrfwp.xxx with different extensions denoting the version
( eg .249 and .270 ). Pick the version you want and copy it onto
a floppy, renaming it to SWXCRFWP.IMA ( IIRC ) when you do. Copy
RA200FL.EXE onto the floppy disk as well. 

   Boot you Alpha into the ARC console. If it's currently SRM you need
to do a "SET OS_TYPE NT" and powercycle the box. Go into setup
(press F2) and select the "Run Utility Program" Option (I think
it's on a submenu called "Maintenance" or something similar ).
Put the floppy in the drive and at the "Program Name" prompt
enter RA200FL. The firmware update should start up and do its
thing.

