On Fri, 4 Jan 2002, Fred Kleinsorge wrote:
> The "^"
> character is not in the filename, but is displayed this way for
> compatability with existing OpenVMS applications.

But by your own admission, the display of "^" is modal.  Thus there is no
way of knowing whether "foo^.bar.zap" means the file "foo.bar.zap" or the
file "foo^.bar.zap".

Nor is there any way to convey the name "foo^.bar.zap" unambiguously to
another program, since "foo^^.bar.zap" and "foo^^^.bar.zap" can mean other
file names.

So, any script that processes names generated by other programs has to
know the mode used by that other program.

You wouldn't have had the problem if you hadn't made the display modal.
This probably means that input is modal as well.

You've already stated that you were obliged to build this kludge tower for
compatibility with the past.  These things happen.  Just admit that this
is a case in which VMS is inferior to UNIX (or even TOPS-20).

