Apple's version is at least better than thr chr ext's, but there are some 
things I don't like about it: four chars is still not enough, and 
type/creator as implemented makes it difficult to distinguish certain 
things that you might want to know -- e.g. postscript files might have a 
bunch of different codes like TEXT/vgrd, TEXT/gsVR, or EPSF/something, so 
it is difficult to know when a TEXT file is actually postscript or when an 
EPSF file could be edited in a text editor.  And I find myself constantly 
changing the creator codes to match who I want to open the file instead of 
who created it.

I'd prefer a system that stored MIME types along with the filename, access 
rights, and other file metadata.
