Julius wrote:

> This is my first foray into the Alpha word and I have a couple of questions
> on the Digital PWS 500a which I am trying to upgrade and install Linux.
> Could some kind soul help answer my questions?  I presume the answers to
> these questions apply to the 500au, 600a and 600au as well.
>
> 1)  Can I upgrade to a faster processor like a 533Mhz or 600Mhz 21164 ?  If
> yes, are there any jumper setting?

You can update the processor, I've heard of people using the 533 and the 600mhz
processors.  I've also heard of people who successfully over clock their
systems too.  The caveat is that you must improve cooling in the system to
accommodate the hotter temps of the processor.  The CPU clock frequency
selection switch bank is located just under processor about halfway to the
riser card connector.  It is an 8 switch bank. The manual that I have does
specify what each switch does, and suggests "Consult the documentation that
comes with the upgrade for instructions on resetting the switches.  Otherwise
do not change the switch settings".  I suspect that it'll be in the FAQ or Ask
The Wizard at the 'Q'.

>
> 2)  Can I use PC based non-ECC SDRAM DIMMs?

No.  ECC is required.  Some PC style DIMMS might work, but could potentially
give problems.  Not worth the time or the the trouble.  Memory is cheap these
days, not like a few years back.

>
> 3)  Will a PC based SCSI controller like the Adaptec 29160 Ultra 160
> controller work on this machine?  If not, which controllers are supported?

Depends on whether you will use AlpaBIOS or SRM.  SRM is quite fussy about SCSI
cards, AlphaBIOS is not quite as bad.  Check around, there's probably a
compatibility list on one of the Alpha Linux web sites.  Alphalinux.org now
http://www.linuxalpha.org will probably have a listing if anybody does.

