The full function CHARON-VAX products emulate a MicroVAX 3600 with 64 MB
memory and include Ethernet adapter emulation (DELQA, DESQA, DEQNA, etc).
There are two emulation models available, the 'traditional' CHARON-VAX and
the 3-5 times faster CHARON-VAX Plus. The latter uses Dynamic Instruction
Translation and runs a bit faster than a VAX 4000/500A on a 1 GHz Pentium
system. You can log into our online CHARON-VAX Plus demo system at
www.vaxemulator.com

It does not make sense to emulate a QDSS or QVSS (would cause lots of
overhead mapping to the graphics on the host system) but you can connect an
Xterminal emulator like the one in Pathworks 32 via Ethernet. On a dual CPU
Windows host you can run the Xterminal emulator in the same box. Performance
is pretty good. Even DECwrite is usable...

Ultrix-32 works fine on both CHARON-VAX for Windows and the OpenVMS/Alpha
host versions; we have several customers running it (they have compilers
only running on Ultrix).

