On 3 Jan 2002, Eric Smith wrote:
> I'm confused.  If you set the version retention to 1, does that mean that
> you keep the latest version and one previous?  Or only the latest?

Only the latest.  To keep the latest version and one previous, set the
retention to 2.

> If you can delete the backup, and then undelete it, does that mean that
> delete doesn't actually  free the space?

That's right.  There's a separate command, EXPUNGE, that frees the space
occupied by all deleted files (and makes those files unrecoverable).  Also
LOGOUT did an implicit EXPUNGE.

Thus on TOPS-20, the "delete file" operation of most other operating
systems is a two-step operation: delete, then expunge.  There is a way to
delete and expunge a file in the same operation, but hardly anyone
actually used it.

This was considered to be a feature.

-- Mark --

