> Multics ( arguably a far more sophisticated and more secure os than
> VMS ) has been ported to the 86x platform. You can buy it as the STOP
> operating system running on XTS-300s ( based on a Pentium 2 )
> It has been evaluated as fulfilling B3 security criteria.
> It is interesting that you can run Unix and DOS programs on it.

The XTS-300 is not a port of Multics. However, the XTS-300 borrowed many
features from Multics. These include its security model, segmented demand
paged virtual memory, and its use of a multi-layer ring structure isolation
mechanism (domains of execution in Intel terminology).

DOS programs do not run on it. It currently provides a UNIX SysV3.2 API and
is iBCS2 compliant. Yes, these are a little dated and we are working on
updating these.

Current information on the XTS-300 can be found at:

http://www.getronicsgov.com/solutions/xts_300.htm

--
