I have an M9301-YA in my 11/34a, too.  There are various things you can tell
it to do by setting the DIP switches, but mine is configured to bring up a $
prompt; at that prompt, I tell it from which media to boot (typically my
RK05s) and off it goes.  In order to get to the $ prompt, I hold down the
CTRL button and press the BOOT button on the programmer's panel.  The RUN
light will come on and stay on.

The documentation says that the 9301 does include a console emulator, and
warns that in order to get it to work the DIP switches must be set right; S3
through S10 should be set to on in order to enable the console emulator.
However, you should also be able to start it by loading its address and
starting there, which makes me wonder if your machine is functional.

The system console port is typically the first in the address space for
SLUs, and according to my manual is at 177560.  The M7856 should indeed be
your console; it typically has the "wrong" gender of plug, and as I recall
just requires a straight gender bend to connect to a terminal (not a null
modem).  Of course, yours could have been rewired at some point....

Good luck!  -- Ian

