one or two such cases out and say "the world would have been like that".

Convince me that the free BSD movements pre-date GNU and I might alter
my stance.  But it is clear RMS's stance came out of that MIT milieu of
the late 60s/early 70s, and the attitudes of the computing world have
never been better than that.  Pity this stuff didn't simply sweep away
all the arrogant clods of Silicone Valley, let alone the Redmond ones
who came after.

GNU was around in embryonic form for a long time before Stallman's
original announcement(s).

