Michael Zarlenga wrote:
> : DCL on RSTS/E has "_" to prevent command symbol substitution.
> 
> Damn shame it never made it to VMS DCL.  Feature like that make
> writing really solid code so much easier.

Not sure about command symbol substitution, but _user will bypass logical name
translation , and I believe forwarding in VMS mail (at least it did in the past).

For instance, if some prankster defined a systemwide logical of your username
to translate to his, if someone sends an email to your name, he will get the
email. But if they send to _yourname, then you will get it.

I would suspect that there are sprinklingof other such behaviours inside VMS.


