peter@abbnm.com (Peter da Silva) writes:
> The GPL is an interesting experiment, but I don't think it's as important
> as people make out. After all, the other free UNIX doesn't seem to be hurt
> by not using it.

Unclear.  The "other free Unix" isn't nearly as popular, and it's not
obvious whether any of that has to do with licensing.  There are some
developers who are willing to contribute to GPL'd projects but not
BSD- or MIT-license projects.  Of course, there are other developers
with the opposite views, and many who will support any "open source"
license.

I would say that the GPL experiment has proven to be reasonably
successful.  However, that doesn't mean that in the absence of the GPL,
another license wouldn't have been as successful.


