complete Oracle set up running on my NT box  ! 

I must confess that the Oracle download is used more for me to study
towards an Oracle certification than for any real development . 
However now if I discuss databases with  clients or  friends,  I
mention Oracle as a viable option for certain applications.

I  know for certain that the IT manager of a  large Sydney based
organisation is going to have a very serious look at using Oracle as a
backend for their online operation almost entirely because of
conversations I had with him in which I spoke of ease of development
using Oracle. Before that they had been considering MS SQL server with
IIS !

Just think of how that could have worked for VMS....

